Z80 JavaScript Instruction-Level Simulator — Full Project Specification
1. Project Overview

This project implements a Z80 microprocessor simulator in JavaScript running inside a web browser. The CPU is emulated at the instruction, register, and bus level. It is not a gate-level simulation. The simulator must:

Execute the full documented Zilog Z80 instruction set (unprefixed, CB, ED, DD, FD).

Model registers, flags, memory, program counter, stack pointer, and index registers.

Simulate instruction fetch, decode, execute cycles.

Visually display all registers and flags.

Show activity on the address bus and data bus.

Load program memory from a user-supplied text file containing address–byte mappings.

Allow the user to run, pause, single-step, and change CPU speed.

Let the user inspect memory when paused.

The final product runs entirely in the browser using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript modules.

