9. Instruction Metadata Schema (Optional for Mass Generation)

Use this schema to generate handlers:
{
  opcode: 0x3E,
  prefix: null,
  mnemonic: "LD A,n",
  length: 2,
  cycles: [7],
  behavior: "A = n; flags unchanged",
  flags: {
    S: "unchanged",
    Z: "unchanged",
    H: "reset",
    P: "parity(result)",
    N: "reset",
    C: "unchanged"
  }
}


10. Sample ROM

This ROM increments A forever. It is ideal for first-run testing.

Assembly

        ORG 0x0000
        LD A,0x00      ; 3E 00
LOOP:   INC A          ; 3C
        JR LOOP        ; 18 FE
        HALT           ; 76


Machine Code
Address	Byte
00000	3E
00001	00
00002	3C
00003	18
00004	FE
00005	76

Text File (for your simulator)
0 3E
1 00
2 3C
3 18
4 FE
5 76

When run:

PC cycles 0 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 2 → …

A increments endlessly 00 → 01 → 02 → … → FF → 00 → …

1. Acceptance Criteria

The simulator is considered correct when:

The sample ROM executes as expected.

Registers and flags update correctly.

Address and data bus values match the actual accesses.

Memory loads properly from text file.

The full documented Z80 instruction set is implemented.

Execution speed is adjustable and stable.

UI correctly reflects CPU state on each update.

Memory viewer is accurate when paused.